From 034f650277eff17878d8536b4c85171c0c456bf0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CanMehEvolve <noreply@example.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Field::GetType: single-return form

What: restructures the early returns into one condition. Behaviour is unchanged.
Why it might be faster: probably it is not; the step measured 0.03% and is noise. Included only because the search accepted it.

Provenance: greedy search, seed 3, generation 18, region 123 (Field::GetType).
Generated by the model (deepseek-v4.1-flash); not hand-written. Search-time ratio R (candidate/stock, <1 is faster): 0.8795 -> 0.8792 at acceptance (max of two measurements). This is a ranking value, NOT an independent per-patch
confirmation; only the fixed FINAL patch of the run was re-measured independently.
Cumulative patch it was derived from: runs/deepseek/greedy-s3-1072869/patches/gen_18.patch (diff against stock; do not apply together with the others).
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/fit_field.cpp | 15 ++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/fit_field.cpp b/src/fit_field.cpp
index 1e4b215..c621405 100644
--- a/src/fit_field.cpp
+++ b/src/fit_field.cpp
@@ -99,13 +99,14 @@ FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
 
 FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
 {
-    if ( type != FIT_UINT8_INVALID )
-        return type;
-
-    if ((profile == NULL) || (profileIndex >= profile->numFields))
-        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;
-
-    return profile->fields[profileIndex].type;
+    if ((type == FIT_UINT8_INVALID) &&
+        (profile != NULL) &&
+        (profileIndex < profile->numFields))
+    {
+        return profile->fields[profileIndex].type;
+    }
+
+    return type;
 }
 
 std::string Field::GetUnits() const
